{"type":"text","timestamp":1794589861955,"sessionID":"ses_e2a20879dffeiHqXeVKCh4T259","part":{"id":"prt_1d5e414d6002zKCNaCC6jZ1KCy","sessionID":"ses_e2a20879dffeiHqXeVKCh4T259","messageID":"msg_1d5e3f100001Xpwo2A5bnfph0x","type":"text","text":"Done. T027 is complete.\n\n## File written\n\n`.opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs` — one new test, `renders the command, its policy and its owner from the advisor row`, placed after the no-brief head test. The scoped diff is the test addition only.\n\nOne deliberate fixture detail beyond the literal snippet: the task's `cliEnvelope({ recommendations: [...] })` carries no `freshness`, and the plugin's `parseCliResponse` maps a missing freshness to `unavailable`, which skips the renderer and yields no brief. I added `freshness: 'live'` so the case renders the row and passes today, as the task requires. This is inferred from the plugin code (`parseCliResponse`), then observed by the passing run.\n\n## Verify output\n\n`VP` (`env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD node --test .opencode/plugins/tests/system-skill-advisor.test.cjs`):\n\n```\nℹ tests 43\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 43\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\n```\n\nBaseline before the edit was 42 pass, 42 tests, so the new case is the +1.\n\n`env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD node TSX $PL/probe-plugin-fields.mts`:\n\n```\ncompiledRouteSummary lines: []\nmetadata readers: [\"1522: const freshness = response.metadata?.freshness;\"]\nbounding jsdoc: [\"1060: * @param {boolean} [rawOptions.boundedCompiledRouteSummary] - Reported as the bounded_comp\"]\nenvelope test inputs with command, policy, ownerSkillId: false, false, false\nplugin test asserts a command label: true\nfallback keeps: command /create:agent, policy start, ownerSkillId sk-doc\nhead: Advisor: live; use sk-doc → /create:agent (start) 0.95/0.12 pass.\n```\n\nThe probe read `plugin test asserts a command label: false` before the edit, which is the negative control for the probe's own check.\n\n## Not done\n\nI did not tick T027 in `tasks.md`. I did not demonstrate the drop-a-field failure by mutating the plugin, because `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` is outside this task's file list and belongs to lane WG6's T025/T026. That the guard fails when `command`, `policy` or `ownerSkillId` is dropped is derived from the literal label assertion, not observed.","time":{"start":1794589856982,"end":1794589861955}}}
